# Observe Flame Blade's conjure form taking the persistent duration, for bd
# inc-wbq9 (PA-07-F9).
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/flame-blade-conjure-duration.keys 1
#
# WHAT IS MEASURED. `flame blade;conjure` creates a `flame blade;weapon` item
# and gives it a SUMMONED stati with duration e.vDuration (src/Effects.cpp:2091,
# CREA_TEMP). Before the fix the effect carried EF_DLONG, so e.vDuration = 100 +
# 10*level and the conjured blade's status line counted down from about 100.
# After the fix it carries EF_PERSISTANT, so e.vDuration is -2 and the status
# line reads "-2 turns" -- the duration that lasts until rest.
#
# THE ORACLE is the status line the moment the blade appears: a positive
# countdown on the pre-fix build, "-2 turns" on the fixed one. This is the
# duration the engine recorded, read from the game's own display.
#
# WHY THE WAIT IS NOT THE ORACLE HERE. A player-conjured blade lands in the
# In-the-Air slot (Character::GainItem, src/Annot.cpp:895-902) and the engine
# drops it when the inventory closes; the weapon's own EV_TURN handler then
# destroys any conjured blade lying on the map (lib/weapons.irh:446-455),
# whatever its duration. So the blade's countdown is read at cast, and the
# persistence across many turns is shown by the augment form, whose quality
# stays on a carried weapon (tools/keys/flame-blade-augment-duration.keys).
@include chargen.keys

# Wizard mode on.
w
y

# Make Flame Blade castable regardless of class.
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Flame Blade"
ENTER

# Cast Flame Blade on self; answer "Augment or conjure? [aC]" with 'c'. Read
# the status line immediately: it shows the conjured blade's recorded duration.
m
@choose "Flame Blade"
c
@dump:after-cast

# Close the inventory manager the cast opened (Character::GainItem,
# src/Annot.cpp:900). The same open/examine/close sequence as the burst script
# returns the game to play mode so the searches below spend game time.
i
b
x
@dump:weapon-after-cast
ESC
ESC

# Pass 200 turns without resting, then look again. On the pre-fix build the
# positive EF_DLONG duration is spent and the blade is gone; on the fixed build
# the blade may also have left the In-the-Air slot when the inventory closed,
# which is why the after-cast line above is the oracle.
@until "HP:" ESC
s*200
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:after-wait

# A full rest advances the day and Map::DaysPassed removes every Duration == -2
# stati (src/Player.cpp:2484/2501), destroying a persistent conjured blade.
@until "HP:" ESC
z
@dump:after-rest

@quit
